// FN-DSA (FIPS 206 draft) over the Falcon-512 parameter set.
//
// SCOPE (SEC-24): this package implements the Falcon-512 verification and
// signing half of FN-DSA. Verification follows the Falcon-512 encoding and
// norm bound. Signing accepts a Falcon-512 private key (f, g, F), recovers G
// modulo q, and samples the signature with the reference Fourier sampler.
// Key generation is not implemented: the required recursive NTRU solver did
// not reach a correct, tested state for this change, and returning a canned
// or unchecked key would be fake output. `publicKeyOf` derives h from an
// existing valid secret key, so signing tests use the published Falcon-512
// known-answer keys.
//
// Randomness is explicit: `sign` expands the caller's 40-byte salt together
// with the message through SHAKE256 and a ChaCha20 PRG, so a signature is a
// pure function of its inputs. Verification is public-data-only and does not
// promise constant time; signing uses secret indices and inherits the
// backend's timing behaviour.
/// The public entry point: verify a padded Falcon-512 signature.
pub pure fn verify(publicKey: Bytes, message: Bytes, signature: Bytes) -> Result[Bool, Error] {
    verifySignature(publicKey, message, signature)
}

/// Deterministically signs `message` with the 40-byte `salt`.
///
/// The signature is a pure function of the secret key, message and salt.
pub pure fn sign(secretKey: Bytes, message: Bytes, salt: Bytes) -> Result[Bytes, Error] {
    signMessage(secretKey, message, salt)
}

/// Derives the Falcon-512 public key from a secret key.
pub pure fn publicKeyOf(secretKey: Bytes) -> Result[Bytes, Error] {
    derivePublicKey(secretKey)
}
